Chrysler ECU (2D) Fuel Calculations

----------

Base Fuel Calculations

In all generations of the Chrysler ECU (LM, SMEC, SBEC at least), the fuel pulsewidth is calculated every Distributor Interrupt. The base pulsewidth is looked up in 1 of 3 tables depending on the throttle condition. There is a base fuel table (no-throttle), a table for part throttle, and a table for full throttle. Then, the computer decides if it should be using starting fuel calculation or running fuel calculat…";}s:8:"relation";a:2:{s:5:"media";a:1:{s:12:"equation.png";b:1;}s:10:"firstimage";s:12:"equation.png";}s:8:"internal";a:2:{s:5:"cache";b:1;s:3:"toc";b:1;}}s:10:"persistent";a:5:{s:4:"date";a:2:{s:7:"created";i:1421704695;s:8:"modified";i:1462927634;}s:11:"last_change";a:7:{s:4:"date";i:1462927634;s:2:"ip";s:13:"23.115.161.12";s:4:"type";s:1:"E";s:2:"id";s:10:"fuel_setup";s:4:"user";s:8:"shelgame";s:3:"sum";s:0:"";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";}s:4:"user";s:0:"";s:7:"creator";s:0:"";s:11:"contributor";a:1:{s:8:"shelgame";s:9:"Rob Lloyd";}}}